adopt-failed	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
agent-failed	try: read the recorded tail in launcher.json, fix the invocation (the agent's own flags go after '--'), then re-run
agent-missing	try: install the agent CLI (or put it on PATH), or re-run with --agent <name> for one you have
agent-record-failed	try: make the bundle directory writable (or re-fetch the bundle), then re-run
agent-spawn-failed	try: check the binary runs from your shell (permissions, shebang), then re-run
agent-timeout	try: re-run with a larger --timeout, or pass the agent's faster flags after '--'
already-adopted	try: use the verb named above for this bundle kind
already-learned	try: cite the existing rule id instead of learning it twice
already-posted	try: re-run with --force to override, or fetch --base-sha <posted-head> for the delta and review it instead — re-fetch if the earlier review was deleted
already-retired	try: check the rule status with learn --status, then re-run
already-reviewed-patch	try: re-run with --force to post the same change again, or fetch the delta/base for a new review
ambiguous-patch-match	try: pass the exact --from <local-slug> named above
ambiguous-sig	try: copy the full sig prefix from report output
approve-blocked	try: triage the findings or re-run with --force
auth-missing	try: export the credential named above, then re-run
backtest-failed	try: confirm git works in this checkout, then re-run
backtest-row-stale	try: delete the named prs/<NNN>/ directory, then replay the run so it records a fresh row
backtest-run-stale	try: re-mine the run in place with the same --run and window, then replay it again
bad-approve	try: pass --approve=true|false
bad-at	try: re-run with one of the valid values named above
bad-attribution	try: re-run with one of the valid values named above
bad-base	try: re-run with one of the valid values named above
bad-budget	try: re-run with one of the valid values named above
bad-by	try: use one of the dimensions named in the message
bad-category	try: re-run with one of the valid values named above
bad-color	try: re-run with one of the valid values named above
bad-config	try: re-run with one of the valid values named above
bad-config-credentials	try: re-run with one of the valid values named above
bad-flags	try: re-run with one of the valid values named above
bad-from	try: re-run with one of the valid values named above
bad-group-validation	try: re-run with one of the valid values named above
bad-id	try: re-run with one of the valid values named above
bad-judgment	try: re-run with one of the valid values named above
bad-lock-source	try: re-run 'verdict pack add <dir|git-url>' from the pack source so .verdict/verdict.lock records a valid source
bad-max-bytes	try: re-run with one of the valid values named above
bad-override	try: re-run with one of the valid values named above
bad-pack	try: fix pack.json against schemas/pack.schema.json (exact lowercase keys, every id paired with its markdown file), then re-run
bad-pack-source	try: use https://host/path with no userinfo, ssh://user@host/path, or user@host:path — a token in the URL, ref, or path is recorded in the committed lock; use an ssh key or a public https URL
bad-panel	try: fix verification/verdicts.json: one result per (sig, model), a known verdict, evidence 10–500 characters
bad-preset	try: re-run with one of the valid values named above
bad-provider	try: re-run with one of the valid values named above
bad-range	try: re-run with one of the valid values named above
bad-reason	try: re-run with one of the valid values named above
bad-requirement	try: re-run with one of the valid values named above
bad-review-input	try: fix the malformed agent input named above (review.json wants {body, approved, comments[]}; claims want string sigs), then re-run
bad-review-schema	try: set "schema_version": "1" in review.json
bad-rigor	try: re-run with one of the valid values named above
bad-root	try: pass --root <existing-directory>, or run serve inside a checkout
bad-rule	try: re-run with one of the valid values named above
bad-scope	try: re-run with one of the valid values named above
bad-settings	try: keep only output/layout/color/publish/review/spend/privacy keys (see docs/manual.md), then re-run
bad-settings-credentials	try: remove the credential key from the settings file (credentials never live there), then re-run
bad-sig	try: list open inline sigs with report --status open --kind inline, then re-run with the full prefix
bad-since	try: pass --since <90d|12w|18mo|2y|ref> (a bare m is not a unit, and the ref must precede --until)
bad-slug	try: re-run with one of the valid values named above
bad-stash	try: re-run with one of the valid values named above
bad-target	try: re-run with one of the valid values named above
bad-timeout	try: pass --timeout <positive-seconds> (default 300)
bad-triage-status	try: re-run with one of the valid values named above
bad-until	try: pass --until <ref> that is an ancestor of HEAD
bad-usage	try: fix the usage record named above to match schemas/usage.schema.json, then re-run
bind-required	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
budget-exceeded	try: re-run with --consent-over-budget once the spend is approved, or raise REVIEW_BUDGET_USD/the typed budget_usd default
budget-unknown	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
bundle-ambiguous	try: address the local bundle as local-<name>; the bare name resolves to a different directory than the discovered one
calibrate-failed	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
canceled	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
chunk-write-failed	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
config-no-bundle	try: run the fetch/record step named above first, then re-run
config-too-large	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
conflicted-tree	try: resolve the conflicts (or abort the merge), then re-run
controls-stale	try: re-fetch the bundle (controls changed under it), then re-run
controls-too-large	try: trim the named control file under its cap, commit it at base, then re-fetch
controls-unavailable	try: check out the PR base (actions/checkout fetch-depth: 0, or git fetch --depth=1 origin <base>), then re-fetch; fetch --allow-head-controls is the explicit opt-out
corpus-invalid	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
corrupt-store	try: re-run post/record to rebuild the store, or restore findings.json from backup, then re-run
cost-entry-contradicts-panel	try: pass the panel in the order it ran (synthesizer first), or fix the entry's name, then re-run
cost-entry-unnamed	try: pass every model that ran: --cost-names=<lead>,<lens-1>,<lens-2>
cost-models-not-array	try: rewrite models as an array of named entries, then re-run
cost-panel-unresolved	try: pass the panel that ran, in order: --cost-names=<lead>,<lens-1>,<lens-2>
cost-unreadable	try: fix or delete the cost record named above, then re-run
coverage-incomplete	try: stamp review.json "coverage": [{"file": "...", "ranges": "1-240"}] for every changed file, or re-run next --coverage to see the gaps, then post again
coverage-stale	try: re-run fetch-local, review the new bundle, then record again
degenerate-body	try: open with a verdict marker (see prompts/review.md), then re-run
diff-failed	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
diff-too-large	try: split the range (--range/--base/--base-sha) or narrow with a paths filter, then re-fetch
download-failed	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
duplicate-payload	try: re-run with --force to repost the identical payload — re-fetch if the earlier review was deleted
fetch-failed	try: run 'gh auth status', confirm the repo/PR spelling, then re-run
fix-ceiling	try: triage the sig or split the fix — the 3-pass ceiling is hard-coded
fix-failed	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
head-mismatch	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
html-not-export	try: choose a new, empty, or previous HTML export directory
html-symlink	try: choose an HTML export directory that is not a symlink
id-taken	try: pass a different --id
index-capped	try: narrow --from/--at to a smaller tree (the 97 MiB git capture cap is fixed; the typed caps cover file, tree and shard bytes only)
index-corrupt	try: delete .verdict/index and rebuild with 'verdict index build'
index-failed	try: delete .verdict/index and rebuild with 'verdict index build'
init-failed	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
internal	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
learn-failed	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
manager-failed	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
manager-missing	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
mcp-config-backup-failed	try: check the config path and permissions named above, then re-run
mcp-config-foreign	try: remove the existing MCP entry by hand, then re-run
mcp-config-no-home	try: set HOME (or CODEX_HOME), then re-run
mcp-config-read-failed	try: check the config path and permissions named above, then re-run
mcp-config-unknown-agent	try: check the config path and permissions named above, then re-run
mcp-config-unmergeable	try: remove the existing MCP entry by hand, then re-run
mcp-config-unparseable	try: fix the JSON/TOML syntax (or move the file aside), then re-run
mcp-config-write-failed	try: check the config path and permissions named above, then re-run
missing-bundle	try: run the fetch/record step named above first, then re-run
missing-chunk-coverage	try: re-fetch the bundle with --chunk, then re-synthesize across all chunks and re-run
missing-chunk-snapshot	try: re-fetch the bundle with --chunk, then re-synthesize across all chunks and re-run
missing-diff	try: run the fetch/record step named above first, then re-run
missing-findings	try: run the fetch/record step named above first, then re-run
missing-index	try: run 'verdict index build' first
missing-patch	try: run the fetch/record step named above first, then re-run
missing-post	try: run the fetch/record step named above first, then re-run
missing-review-file	try: run the fetch/record step named above first, then re-run
missing-sig	try: run the fetch/record step named above first, then re-run
missing-source	try: run the fetch/record step named above first, then re-run
missing-tool	try: run the fetch/record step named above first, then re-run
needs-confirm	try: re-run with --yes after reviewing the preview, then re-run
no-patch-match	try: pass --from <local-slug>, or re-fetch the target bundle so identity.json exists
no-pr-target	try: run the fetch/record step named above first, then re-run
no-review-artifact	try: run the printed command yourself (--print) to see why no review.json appeared, then re-run
no-run-bundle	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
no-threads	try: run the fetch/record step named above first, then re-run
no-verify-cmd	try: run the fetch/record step named above first, then re-run
not-a-repo	try: run the fetch/record step named above first, then re-run
not-local	try: run the fetch/record step named above first, then re-run
not-retired	try: check the rule status with learn --status, then re-run
not-verdict-authored	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
pack-conflict	try: add "replace": ["<lower pack name>"] to the higher pack's manifest, or rename the conflicting id
pack-git-failed	try: check the source URL, the ref, your access, and the network, then re-run
pack-lock-drift	try: re-add the pack with 'verdict pack add <dir|git-url>' so .verdict/verdict.lock records its current tree hash
pack-lock-missing	try: run 'verdict pack add <dir|git-url>' to vendor the pack and write its .verdict/verdict.lock entry
pack-staging-stale	try: delete the dot-prefixed sibling under .verdict/packs/ that the message names by hand (its permissions block the sweep), then re-run
pack-test-cases	try: add evals/<case>/diff.patch, findings.json, and expect.json to the pack, then re-run 'verdict pack test'
pack-too-large	try: trim the pack under 64 KiB per file, 1 MiB total, 256 files, and 64 lenses, then re-run
pack-unsafe-path	try: keep every pack path relative with no symlink components, then re-run
panel-empty	try: configure defaults.panel with a synthesizer and verifiers, re-fetch, then re-run panel
panel-stale	try: re-run verification/dispatch.md against the current bundle head and rewrite verification/verdicts.json
panel-too-large	try: narrow the review or roster (100 findings, 4 verifiers maximum), then re-run panel
post-failed	try: narrow anchor drift or body size (see above), then re-run
post-secret-shaped	try: remove the value from review.json and re-run, or pass --allow-secret-values to publish it anyway
pr-not-open	try: re-fetch the PR (bundle may be stale)
pr-read-failed	try: run 'gh auth status', confirm the repo/PR spelling, then re-run
privacy-unavailable	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
prompt-dump-failed	try: run from a checkout carrying SKILL.md/prompts, then re-run
provider-unimplemented	try: use the verb named above for this bundle kind
rationale-required	try: add --rationale with 30+ chars, or --force
record-failed	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
repair-exhausted	try: fix every error named in error.problems, then re-run (when the cap was hit, raise --rounds up to 5; for no progress check the round files)
report-failed	try: run the fetch/record step named above first, then re-run
requirement-blocked	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
requirement-unmet	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
rounds-path-unsafe	try: remove the named path from the bundle (verdict owns it as a plain directory), then re-run
run-mismatch	try: pick another --run, or delete the existing run directory
sandbox-unavailable	try: install bubblewrap on Linux and allow unprivileged user namespaces, or re-run without --sandbox on a command you trust
scope-escape	try: revert or stash files outside the anchor path, then re-run fix
serve-listen-failed	try: pass --port 0 for a kernel-assigned port, or free the named address, then re-run
skill-bad-dir	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
skill-dir-foreign	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
skill-foreign-conflict	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
skill-install-failed	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
skill-no-detected-agent	try: name the agent explicitly with 'verdict skill install --agent <name>'
skill-no-home	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
skill-not-installed	try: install first with 'verdict skill install --dir <skills-dir>', or check the target
skill-path-not-inventory	try: run 'verdict skill files' to list every embedded path
skill-read-failed	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
skill-target-file	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
skill-unknown-agent	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
spend-capped	try: re-run with --consent-over-budget once the spend is approved, or raise the personal spend ceiling (spend.budget_usd) in the operator settings, then re-run
stale-review-artifact	try: delete the stale review.json (or let the agent overwrite it), then re-run
threads-failed	try: run 'gh auth status', confirm the repo/PR spelling, then re-run
triage-failed	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
uninstall-foreign	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
uninstall-no-receipt	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
unknown-agent	try: re-run with one of the known agent names listed above
unknown-group	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
unknown-judgment	try: copy the full sig prefix from report output
unknown-rule	try: list rules with learn --status, then re-run
unknown-sig	try: copy the full sig prefix from report output
unknown-thread	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
unsupported-cap	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
unsupported-platform	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
upgrade-bad-method	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
upgrade-bad-version	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
upgrade-failed	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
upgrade-needs-privilege	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
upgrade-project-local	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
upgrade-skill-copy	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
upgrade-unidentified	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
upgrade-version-unsupported	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
upstream-diff-too-large	try: re-fetch narrowed to a range via --base-sha/--since, or narrow with a paths filter, then re-run
verify-credential-read	try: rewrite verifyCmd without reading credential paths or piping env into the network, then re-run
verify-destructive	try: rewrite verifyCmd to stay in-repo and non-destructive (run the test runner, not rm/mkfs/dd), then re-run
verify-failed	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
verify-networked	try: rewrite verifyCmd without network fetches or pipe-to-shell (fetch fixtures first, run offline), then re-run
verify-repo-escape	try: rewrite verifyCmd with repo-relative paths (/tmp for scratch), then re-run
window-too-large	try: narrow --since (a shorter span or a later ref), then re-run
worktree-failed	try: address the cause above, then re-run the same command
